<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Did the Heat Extend Andrew Wiggins?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Wiggins is paid <strong>$30.17m</strong> because a first overall pick who became a starter on a championship team keeps a large number long after the draft.</p>
<ul>
<li>Minnesota gave him <strong>$147.71m</strong> over five years in 2017, before he had made an All-Star team.</li>
<li>He won the championship with Golden State in 2022 and was extended for <strong>$109m</strong> that summer.</li>
<li>He was an All-Star in 2022, the only time in thirteen seasons.</li>
<li>He exercised a player option on this season, which is what a player does when the market is thinner than the deal.</li>
<li>Miami has already agreed to pay him <strong>$33.83m</strong> more after it ends.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has been paid <strong>$281.56m</strong> and made one All-Star team.</p>

